{"v":1,"accession":"PRJDB8489","title":"Anodic biofilms on a bioelectrochemical system-based trickling filter bioreactor","description":"In this study, we proposed an aerobic bioelectrochemical system (BES)-based trickling filter (TF) bioreactor for current generation and wastewater treatment. The wastewater treatment efficiencies of this bioreactor were also evaluated. It is important to understand the mechanism of community-structure formation, therefore, the microbial communities on the whole carbon fiber anode (CFA) were investigated. Reactor 1 (R1) and reactor 2 (R2) were set up in duplicates. For each reactor, 5 samples of biofilms taken from different sites were analyzed for each reactor, which were biofilms for the planktonic-cell fraction in the solution of the reactor (PC), biofilms on the outer part of the lower anode (Outer-Low), biofilms on the outer part of the upper anode without immersion (Outer-Up), biofilms in the inner layer of the lower anode (Inner-Low), and biofilms in the inner layer of the upper anode without immersion (Inner-Up). The microbial community on the CFA was analyzed using Illumina high throughput sequencing targeting on amplicons of 16S rRNA gene.","center":"Kanazawa University","data_type":"Other","submission_date":"2020/07/09 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMD00177022","biofilms for the planktonic-cell fraction in the solution of the reactor 1","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater",null,2018,"JP","Ishikawa",null,null,"unresolved",null,null,"Japan:Ishikawa",null,null,null,"biofilm","city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMD00177023","biofilms for the planktonic-cell fraction in the solution of the reactor 2","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater",null,201